From 6a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Security Engineer <security@example.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Limit recursion depth during XInclude processing

Added a maximum include depth constant (MAX_INCLUDE_DEPTH = 128) to
prevent stack exhaustion from deeply nested imports. The depth is
tracked via a counter in the XmlReadOptions struct. If the limit is
exceeded during loading, an exception is thrown instead of recursing
further.

This addresses CVE-2025-53011 by enforcing a cap on the import chain
depth. A depth of 128 is sufficient for legitimate use cases while
preventing controlled stack overflow attacks.

